      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-310826",
      ":question/problem": "For the exponential function $f$, the value of $f(0)$ is $c$, where $c$ is a constant. Of the following equations that define the function $f$, which equation shows the value of $c$ as the coefficient or the base?\n\n1. $f(x) = 22 \\cdot (1.5)^{x + 1}$\n2. $f(x) = 33 \\cdot (1.5)^{x}$\n3. $f(x) = 49.5 \\cdot (1.5)^{x - 1}$\n4. $f(x) = 74.25 \\cdot (1.5)^{x - 2}$"
